Package: davinci-aac-support
Version: __VERSION__
Section: video
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3, ffmpeg, systemd, curl
Recommends: libnotify-bin
Maintainer: Josh Bosley
Homepage: https://github.com/broskisworld/davinci-aac-support
Description: Fixes DaVinci Resolve's silent AAC audio import bug on Linux
 Installs a background watcher that detects AAC audio DaVinci Resolve
 can't decode on Linux and re-encodes it to PCM in place, so imported
 clips just work. The setup window opens automatically right after
 install to finish the one-time per-user step (the watcher itself runs
 as your own systemd --user service, not a system daemon, so it can't
 be started as part of the package install itself). If it doesn't
 appear, open "DaVinci AAC Support" from your applications menu instead.
